<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# data-theme="dark" is load-bearing, not decoration.

    brgen's :root includes brgen-old-dark-tokens and has done all along, but
    shared/_tokens.scss ends with

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
        :root:not([data-theme="dark"]) { ...light palette... }
      }

    and `:root:not(...)` outranks a bare `:root`. So on any client whose OS
    prefers light — the default on most installs — that block won and brgen
    rendered light: measured on the live site as --bg #f7f6fa against the
    #17161c its own root declares, with the theme toggle sitting unchecked.
    Every vertical inherits this layout, so all six surfaces were affected.

    Claiming the opt-out the shared system already provides fixes it without
    touching shared CSS. The explicit toggle is unaffected: it switches through
    `#dark-toggle:checked ~ .theme-root`, a different selector, so a visitor who
    asks for light still gets light.

    The value is per vertical, not a constant (operator, 2026-08-24). It was
    hardcoded "dark" for every surface, so markedsplass, maps and takeaway --
    the three that are designed light -- rendered on the dark palette while
    their accents stayed tuned for the light one. ApplicationHelper#surface_theme
    holds the mapping. %>
<html lang="<%= Current.locale || I18n.locale %>" dir="ltr" data-theme="<%= surface_theme %>" class="chrome-hidden">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <%= tag.meta name: "viewport", content: "width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" %>
  <%= tag.meta name: "mobile-web-app-capable", content: "yes" %>
  <%# iOS ignores the manifest for standalone behaviour — these give an installed
      iPhone a real full-screen app, a translucent status bar, and a branded name. %>
  <%= tag.meta name: "apple-mobile-web-app-capable", content: "yes" %>
  <%= tag.meta name: "apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style", content: "black-translucent" %>
  <%= tag.meta name: "apple-mobile-web-app-title", content: city_name %>
  <%= tag.meta name: "color-scheme", content: "dark" %>
  <%= tag.meta name: "theme-color", content: "#000000", data: { light_color: "#ffffff", dark_color: "#000000" } %>
  <%# Must run before first paint and before any stylesheet, which is why it is a
      blocking inline script here rather than a Stimulus controller: theme-toggle
      is mounted on <body> and only reaches the DOM after Stimulus boots, so a
      visitor with "light" saved was served a dark first frame on every load.
      WIRING_NOTES.md has described this partial as the FOUC guard the whole time
      nothing rendered it. %>
  <%= render "shared/theme_bootstrap", storage_key: "brgen-theme" %>
  <%# content_for(:x) with no block is the read form: it already returns nil when unset,
      so content_for?(:x) ? yield(:x) : … was two lookups and the key named twice. %>
  <% page_title = content_for(:title).presence %>
  <% page_description = content_for(:description).presence || t("pages.default_description", city: city_name) %>
  <title><%= page_title ? "#{page_title} — #{city_name}" : city_name %></title>
  <meta name="description" content="<%= page_description %>">
  <link rel="canonical" href="<%= request.original_url.split("?").first %>">
  <%= render "layouts/social_card_meta", page_title: page_title, page_description: page_description %>
  <link rel="preload" href="/icon.png" as="image">
  <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">
  <%= tag.link rel: "manifest", href: main_app.pwa_manifest_path(format: :json) %>
  <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
  <%= csp_meta_tag %>
  <%= yield :head %>
  <%# Brand fonts are self-hosted (see _fonts_brand.scss); preload only the face
      this surface actually uses so it is ready before first text paint. %>
  <% if active_vertical.in?(%i[dating maps messenger]) %>
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="/fonts/inter-latin-400-normal.woff2" crossorigin>
  <% elsif active_vertical == :marketplace && File.file?(Rails.root.join("public/fonts/pp-neue-montreal-latin-700-normal.woff2")) %>
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="/fonts/pp-neue-montreal-latin-700-normal.woff2" crossorigin>
  <% end %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lightgallery.css">
  <meta name="lg-license" content="<%= ENV.fetch("LIGHTGALLERY_LICENSE", "0000-0000-000-0000") %>">
  <%= yield :json_ld %>
  <%= json_ld_script(organization_json_ld(site_name: city_name, url: main_app.root_url, area_served: city_name)) %>
  <%= json_ld_script(website_json_ld(site_name: city_name, url: main_app.root_url, description: page_description, search: !vertical_surface?, area_served: city_name)) %>
  <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
</head>
<body class="<%= body_surface_classes %>"
      data-layout="document"
      data-surface="social"
      data-controller="feed-hotkey browser-fingerprint brgen-shell battery-aware network-aware"
      data-feed-hotkey-help-value="<%= t("hotkeys.help") %>"
      data-feed-hotkey-coach-value="<%= t("hotkeys.coach") %>"
      data-feed-hotkey-coach-dismiss-value="<%= t("hotkeys.coach_dismiss") %>"
      data-browser-fingerprint-url-value="<%= main_app.fingerprint_path %>"
      <%= yield(:body_attrs) if content_for?(:body_attrs) %>>
  <%# Every surface, playlist included. The skip link must be the first focusable
      element on the page or it cannot do its job. The playlist tunnel used to
      opt out because the pill painted as a light rectangle in the brand corner;
      _shell.scss now clips it to 1×1 with clip-path + opacity:0 (see the comment
      at the top of that file, which names this tunnel), so there is nothing left
      to paint. %>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content"><%= t("skip_to_content") %></a>
  <%# After the skip link, not before it — the sprite is inert (aria-hidden,
      focusable="false", 0x0) so it cannot take focus either way, but the rule
      above is that nothing precedes the skip link. %>
  <%= render "shared/icon_sprite" if icon_sprite? %>
  <%# <header> only to give the wordmark a banner landmark — axe's region rule
      flagged it as the one piece of page content outside any landmark. It adds
      no box: .brgen-logo-mark is position:fixed, so the header has no in-flow
      child and computes to zero height, and every rule that styles the mark
      selects it by class with no combinator, so none of them can notice a new
      parent. Do not hang layout off this element. %>
  <%# One shared mark across brgen, amber and bsdports (shared/_brand_mark).
      class_name keeps .brgen-logo-mark so every rule already written against it
      -- including _vertical_shell's playlist case -- still applies. %>
  <%# label/prefix/suffix come from brand_mark_fragments so the mark names the
      host: "brgen" on the apex, "markedsplass.brgen.no" on a vertical, and the
      city's own name on every other city host. %>
  <%= render "shared/brand_mark", **brand_mark_fragments, class_name: "brand-mark brgen-logo-mark" %>
  <% unless vertical_surface? %>
    <div role="region" aria-label="<%= t("theme.region") %>">
<%# The one theme mechanism: the shared toggle writes data-theme through
    the Stimulus controller, and the shared bootstrap restores it at
    parse time so a saved light theme does not flash dark first. The
    checkbox-sibling CSS lane this layout used to carry is gone — the
    dataset is authoritative in every app. %>
<%= render "shared/theme_bootstrap", storage_key: "brgen-theme" %>
<%= render "shared/theme_toggle", storage_key: "brgen-theme" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="theme-root" data-controller="bottom-sheet">
  <%= render "shared/nav_swiper" %>
  <div id="nearby-alerts" class="nearby-alerts" data-turbo-permanent aria-live="polite"></div>
  <div id="match-overlays" data-turbo-permanent aria-live="polite"></div>
  <div data-controller="geolocation"
       data-geolocation-url-value="<%= main_app.location_path %>"
       data-geolocation-radius-km-value="10"
       data-turbo-permanent></div>
  <% if Current.user %>
    <%= turbo_stream_from "nearby_alerts_#{Current.user.id}" %>
    <%= turbo_stream_from "brgen:matches:#{Current.user.id}" %>
    <%# DMs only — public channels are ambient and must not light the badge.
        One COUNT, not a Ruby sum over 2 queries per thread on every render of
        every page. The filter lives in unread_total_for. %>
    <% unread = Conversation.unread_total_for(Current.user) %>
    <div data-controller="push"
         data-push-vapid-key-value="<%= Shared::Vapid.public_key %>"
         data-push-subscribe-url-value="<%= main_app.push_subscriptions_path %>"
         data-push-unread-value="<%= unread %>"
         data-turbo-permanent></div>
    <button id="push-enable-btn" class="push-enable-btn" hidden><%= t("push.enable") %></button>
  <% end %>

  <%# Only apexes that serve. This list used to be 29 domains written out here;
      26 of them refused the connection and one, amstrdam.nl, had left us and
      redirected to a stranger's site. DomainRegistry::LIVE_DOMAINS is the one
      place that fact is recorded — do not iterate ENTRIES here. %>
  <% live_cities = Brgen::DomainRegistry.live_entries %>
  <% if live_cities.length > 1 %>
    <div id="cityCarousel" class="city-carousel" data-turbo-permanent aria-label="<%= t("nav.city_network") %>" data-brgen-shell-target="carousel">
      <div class="carousel-container" role="list">
        <% live_cities.each do |entry| %>
          <a class="carousel-slide<%= " active" if entry.domain == Current.domain %>" role="listitem"
             href="https://<%= entry.domain %>/" data-domain="<%= entry.domain %>" data-base="<%= entry.domain %>"><%= entry.domain %></a>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="app-shell" data-controller="scroll-chrome" data-scroll-chrome-storage-key-value="pub4:tab-bar:open">
    <div class="layout">
      <%# intro: the sidebar starts revealed for a first-time visitor and stays
          the swipe-reveal drawer after the first dismissal — visible until
          known, hidden once learned (operator, 2026-08-22). %>
      <div class="sidebar-swiper" data-controller="edge-swiper" data-edge-swiper-edge-value="left" data-edge-swiper-intro-value="brgen-sidebar" data-turbo-permanent>
      <aside class="sidebar" aria-label="<%= t("nav.sidebar") %>" data-edge-swiper-target="root">
        <nav data-turbo-permanent aria-label="<%= t("nav.primary_nav") %>">
          <% nav_cls = ->(path) { "nav-item#{" active" if current_page?(path)}" } %>
<%# Chunked, not shortened. Hick's law is about peers at one decision
    level: ten flat entries is the number the reader faces, four
    labelled groups is between one and four. The split follows the
    order the nav already had — discovery, then the inbox, then the
    city, then the account — so nothing is reordered and no entry
    changes meaning. role=group carries it to assistive tech, and
    _shell.scss gives .nav-group display: contents so the nav's own
    flex column still lays the items out and nothing moves. %>
          <div class="nav-group" role="group" aria-label="<%= t("nav.group_discover") %>">
          <%= link_to main_app.root_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.root_path) do %>
            <%= icon :home, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.home") %>
          <% end %>
          <%= render "shared/ai_nav_link" %>
          <%= link_to main_app.communities_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.communities_path) do %>
            <%= icon :explore, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.explore") %>
          <% end %>
          <%= link_to main_app.global_search_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.global_search_path) do %>
            <%= icon :search, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.search") %>
          <% end %>
          </div>
          <div class="nav-group" role="group" aria-label="<%= t("nav.group_inbox") %>">
          <%= link_to main_app.notifications_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.notifications_path) do %>
            <%= icon :notifications, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.notifications") %>
          <% end %>
          <%= link_to main_app.conversations_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.conversations_path) do %>
            <%= icon :messages, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.messages") %>
          <% end %>
          </div>
          <div class="nav-group" role="group" aria-label="<%= t("nav.group_city") %>">
          <%= link_to main_app.nearby_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.nearby_path) do %>
            <%= icon :nearby, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.nearby") %>
          <% end %>
          <%= link_to main_app.events_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.events_path) do %>
            <%= icon :calendar, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.events") %>
          <% end %>
          <%= link_to main_app.stories_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.stories_path) do %>
            <%= icon :camera, size: 26 %>
            <%= t("nav.stories") %>
          <% end %>
          </div>
          <div class="nav-group" role="group" aria-label="<%= t("nav.group_account") %>">
          <% if authenticated? %>
            <%= link_to main_app.user_path(Current.user), class: nav_cls.(main_app.user_path(Current.user)) do %>
              <%= icon :profile, size: 26 %>
              <%= t("nav.profile") %>
            <% end %>
          <% else %>
            <%= link_to main_app.new_session_path, class: nav_cls.(main_app.new_session_path) do %>
              <%= icon :sign_in, size: 26 %>
              <%= t("nav.sign_in") %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
          </div>
        </nav>
        <% if authenticated? %>
          <div class="sidebar-dropdown" data-controller="dropdown" data-action="click@window->dropdown#hide">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" data-dropdown-button aria-expanded="false" data-action="click->dropdown#toggle"><%= t("nav.more") %></button>
            <div class="sidebar-dropdown-menu hidden" data-dropdown-target="menu">
              <%= link_to t("nav.profile"), main_app.user_path(Current.user) %>
              <%= link_to t("nav.new_post"), main_app.new_post_path %>
              <%= link_to t("nav.new_community"), main_app.new_community_path %>
              <%= link_to t("nav.sign_out"), main_app.session_path, data: { turbo_method: :delete, turbo_prefetch: false } %>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <a href="<%= main_app.new_post_path %>" class="compose-btn">
          <%= icon :compose, size: 22, css_class: "compose-icon" %>
          <span class="compose-label"><%= t("nav.post") %></span>
        </a>
      </aside>
      <button type="button" class="edge-grip edge-grip-start" data-edge-swiper-target="grip"
              data-action="click->edge-swiper#toggle" aria-label="<%= t("nav.show_sidebar") %>" aria-expanded="false"></button>
      </div>

      <main id="main-content" aria-label="<%= t("nav.main") %>" data-controller="pull-to-refresh">
        <% if !vertical_surface? && current_page?(main_app.root_path) %>
          <div class="feed-header">
            <%# Visual brand is the fixed top-left .brgen-logo-mark (all surfaces).
                No .feed-tabs row here. It listed subapp_nav_items -- exactly the
                seven verticals brgen_nav_groups already puts in the always-visible
                .nav_swiper_bar directly above it. Two sticky horizontal scrollers
                at top:0 showing the same seven destinations read as two nav
                swipers, cost 104px of chrome on a 997px page, and pushed the first
                feed item to y:128. The swiper is the canonical primary nav
                (WIRING_NOTES "Layout"); this row was the duplicate. %>
            <h1 class="visually-hidden"><%= t("nav.home") %></h1>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <%# City feed + compose first. AI lives as a compact chip in the home
            intro (and full-page via ?master=1), not as an eager above-fold hero
            that pushed "Bergen, right now" and guest paths below the fold. %>
        <% if current_page?(main_app.root_path) && Current.user.present? %>
          <%= render "shared/feed_compose" %>
        <% end %>
        <% if notice.present? %>
          <p role="status" class="flash-notice" aria-live="polite"><%= notice %></p>
        <% end %>
        <% if alert.present? %>
          <p role="alert" class="flash-alert" aria-live="assertive"><%= alert %></p>
        <% end %>
        <%= yield %>
      </main>

      <%= render "shared/widgets_rail" %>
    </div>

    <%= render "shared/mobile_chrome" %>
  </div>
  </div>
  <%= render "shared/install_prompt",
        title: t("install.title"),
        body: t("install.body") %>
  <%= render "shared/nearby_chat_widget" %>
  <%= render "shared/link_converter" %>
  <%= render "shared/site_legal_footer" %>
</body>
</html>
